AGaMEMnon is an open SDK, FPGA toolchain, and English documentation for
the AGM AG32 RISC-V MCU with embedded AGRV2K fabric.

This is IceStorm for a chip nobody has heard of. Verilog synthesizes,
places, routes, and runs on real silicon: combinational and sequential
logic, counters and state machines, clocking across the array, output
to real pins, and the RISC-V core reading and writing the fabric over
its memory bus.

Features:
- Complete reverse-engineering of the vendor af.exe tool
- Yosys -> nextpnr -> bitgen flow for FPGA fabric
- RISC-V GCC toolchain for MCU firmware
- OpenOCD programming via SWD/DAP
- Silicon-validated on AG32VF303-L48
